#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# group_blocks

#% text
# `group_blocks(G), (G, [p, q])`: a block system with the least nontrivial blocks (the minimal one with p and q in one block)

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The minimal block containing two points is found by Atkinson's union-find algorithm. A primitive group gives one block of all points.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
group_blocks(dihedral_group(6))
#% output
#= [[1, 4], [2, 5], [3, 6]]

#% cell
group_blocks(dihedral_group(6), [1, 3])
#% output
#= [[1, 3, 5], [2, 4, 6]]

#% cell
group_blocks(dihedral_group(7))
#% output
#= [[1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7]]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `is_primitive`, `is_transitive`
